From 1ab5b7392747771970ce0a279e709f3f3d4b252a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Cl=C3=A9ment=20Gayot?= <contact@clement-gayot.fr>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:52:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: support GNOME Shell 51

GNOME Shell 51 removed three APIs the extension relies on
(https://gjs.guide/extensions/upgrading/gnome-shell-51.html):

- ui/pointerWatcher.js: still import it on GNOME Shell 50 and earlier;
  on 51, follow the pointer through the cursor tracker's
  position-invalidated signal instead, as ui/magnifier.js now does
  (CursorTrackerPointerWatcher).  The signal is not used on older
  versions: before mutter 50 it was not emitted for captured input.
- Clutter.get_default_backend(): get the seat from
  global.stage.context.get_backend() instead (getDefaultSeat).
- Shell.GLSLEffect: on GNOME Shell 51, GammaCurveEffect derives from
  Clutter.ShaderEffect, which takes the GLSL as a Cogl snippet and sets
  uniforms by name.  GNOME Shell 45-50 keep the GLSLEffect
  implementation; only the class matching the running Shell is
  registered.

Add "51" to shell-version.
